# Public env for AuraHUD
#
# GitHub Pages (current host)
# 1. Repo → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → Variables
# 2. Add:
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL   (https://<user>.github.io/<repo> or your custom domain)
#      NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH  (optional; defaults to /<repo>. Use "/" for a custom domain)
# 3. Settings → Pages → Source: GitHub Actions
# 4. In Supabase → Authentication → URL Configuration, allow the Pages origin
#    and /auth/callback/ redirect.
#
# Required
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
#
# Public site URL (invite links)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-user.github.io/your-repo
#
# Optional Doppler (only if you still run a Node host for Plaid/cron)
# Backend Supabase key (server-only; never expose to the browser)
# Prefer the new secret key from Supabase → Settings → API Keys
# (Publishable and secret API keys tab) — looks like sb_secret_...
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_...
# Legacy fallback (optional): SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJ...
# Signs short-lived application security grants (REQUIRED; dedicated random value)
# Do not reuse the Supabase secret/service-role key here.
# APP_SECURITY_SECRET=long-random-secret
#
# ── Plaid bank sync (not available on GitHub Pages) ──
# From https://dashboard.plaid.com → Team Settings → Keys
# PLAID_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id
# PLAID_SECRET=your_sandbox_or_development_secret
# PLAID_ENV=sandbox
# Encrypts stored access tokens (REQUIRED; dedicated random value)
# Do not reuse CRON_SECRET — rotating cron auth would break decrypt.
# BANK_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=long-random-secret
# CRON_SECRET=long-random-secret
#
# Sandbox test credentials in Plaid Link: user_good / pass_good
